{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.SkeinResolutionObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.SkeinResolutionObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Prod"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.descartes_kummer_persistence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.descartes_kummer_persistence","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L282-L287","doc":"For the Descartes universe (χ = -6), the obstruction persists\nat all levels n where n does not divide 6. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.infinitely_many_non_divisors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.infinitely_many_non_divisors","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L269-L280","doc":"There are infinitely many levels where the obstruction persists:\nfor any degree d > 0, the set {n : ¬ n | d} is infinite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.kummerVanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.kummerVanishes","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L264-L267","doc":"The Kummer divisibility condition: the obstruction at level n\nvanishes iff n divides the Skein degree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.finite_field_bounded_weights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.finite_field_bounded_weights","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L233-L237","doc":"The resolution tree over a finite field has finitely many\ndistinct weights, bounded by the field size. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.finite_decidable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.finite_decidable","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L223-L231","doc":"Over a finite type with decidable equality, every function is\ncomputable: one can evaluate it by enumeration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.skein_perpetual_an","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.skein_perpetual_an","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L207-L216","doc":"If the analytic component (residual weight) is nonzero,\nthe total obstruction is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.skein_perpetual_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.skein_perpetual_top","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L194-L205","doc":"**Perpetual obstruction for the Skein resolution (concrete).**\n\nIf the topological component (Skein degree) is nonzero,\nthe total obstruction is nonzero in the product decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.realProductDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.realProductDecomposition","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L175-L192","doc":"The standard complementary decomposition on ℝ × ℝ\n(product of two copies, intersection is the origin). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ObstructionData.total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ObstructionData.total","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L173-L173","doc":"The total obstruction: their sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ObstructionData.analytic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ObstructionData.analytic","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L171-L171","doc":"The analytic component: residual tree weight at q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ObstructionData.topological","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ObstructionData.topological","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L169-L169","doc":"The topological component: Skein polynomial degree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ObstructionData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ObstructionData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L167-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ObstructionData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ObstructionData","kind":"structure","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L164-L173","doc":"The obstruction decomposition over ℝ: the topological component\nis a constant (the Skein degree), and the analytic component\nis the residual tree weight at parameter q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.perpetual_obstruction_both","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.perpetual_obstruction_both","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L139-L149","doc":"**Perpetual obstruction (both nonzero).**\n\nWhen both components are nonzero and live in complementary\nsubspaces, the sum is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.perpetual_obstruction_an","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.perpetual_obstruction_an","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L121-L137","doc":"**Perpetual obstruction (analytic nonzero).**\n\nSymmetric version: if the analytic component is nonzero,\nthe total element is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.perpetual_obstruction_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.perpetual_obstruction_top","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L90-L119","doc":"**Perpetual obstruction (algebraic core).**\n\nIf an element decomposes into topological and analytic components,\nand either component is nonzero, and the subspaces are complementary,\nthen the total element is nonzero.\n\nThis was written to mirror QU-to-QOU theorem item 3 (κ₀ and δₙ in\ncomplementary subgroups, so κₙ = κ₀ + δₙ ≠ 0). The algebraic lemma here is\nunaffected, but that reading of item 3 is withdrawn: on Bring's surface the\nobstruction vanishes for `n ∣ χ = -6` (re-scoped 2026-11-15, owner decision,\nPR #7747, bean `qou-lx8f`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.complementary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.complementary","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L83-L83","doc":"**Complementarity**: the intersection is trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The decomposition sums to the original. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.snd_an","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.snd_an","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Second component is analytic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.fst_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.fst_top","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L77-L77","doc":"First component is topological. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.decompose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.decompose","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Every element decomposes uniquely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.an_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.an_neg","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.top_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.top_neg","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Subspace closure under negation within each component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.an_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.an_add","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.top_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.top_add","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Subspace closure under addition within each component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.an_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.an_zero","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.top_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.top_zero","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Zero is in both subspaces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.analytic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.analytic","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The analytic subspace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.topological","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.topological","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The topological subspace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.ComplementaryDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/skein-resolution-obstruction.lean#L58-L83","doc":"A direct sum decomposition of an additive group into two complementary\nsubgroups.  Elements from different summands cannot cancel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SkeinResolutionObstruction.q_inv_param","k